LOCATION:Fine Arts Building\, 1201 East 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
GEO:39.169084;-86.518997
SUMMARY:Michael Berryhill: good sad happy bad | Lecture
DESCRIPTION:For painter Michael Berryhill\, there's no difference bet
 ween realism and abstraction. His work reminds the viewer of the challeng
 e of capturing the process of painting\, and the physical and conceptual 
 layering that a surface might contain.Berryhill has had solo exhibition
 s at Night Gallery in Los Angeles and at both Kate Werble and Derek Ell
 er galleries in New York City and been reviewed in The New York Times\, H
 yperallergic\, Art in America\, Artforum\, The Brooklyn Rail\, Modern Pai
 nters\, Huffington Post\, Time Out NY\, Artnet News\, Flaunt magazine\,�
 �Whitehot Magazine of Contemporary Art\, L Magazine\, and artcritical.B
 erryhill earned his M.F.A. from Columbia University and has held visiting
  faculty positions at Bard\, Columbia\, Pratt\, and VCU. Berryhill was 
 Dean of Skowhegan School of Painting and Sculpture for two years. He was 
 artist-in-residence at the University of Tennessee\, Knoxville and Virgin
 ia Commonwealth University in Richmond\, Virginia and held the Painting's
  Edge Residency at Idyllwild Arts Academy in California. He received a Ne
 w York Foundation for the Arts Fellowship for Painting and was a Studio S
 pace recipient at the Marie Walsh Sharpe Art Foundation.Born in El Paso
 \, Texas\, Michael Berryhill earned his undergraduate degree at Univers
 ity of Texas Austin. He lives and works in Ellenville\, New York.Artist's
  instagram:  @berryhillmichael 
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p class="p1"><span class="s1">For painter M
 ichael Berryhill\, there's no difference between realism and abstract
 ion. His work reminds the viewer of the challenge of capturing the proces
 s of painting\, and the physical and conceptual layering that a surface m
 ight contain.</span></p><p class="p1"><span class="s1">Berryhill has ha
 d solo exhibitions at Night Gallery in Los Angeles and at both Kate Wer
 ble and Derek Eller galleries in New York City and been reviewed in The N
 ew York Times\, Hyperallergic\, Art in America\, Artforum\, The Brooklyn 
 Rail\, Modern Painters\, Huffington Post\, Time Out NY\, Artnet News\, Fl
 aunt magazine\, Whitehot Magazine of Contemporary Art\, L Magazine\, 
 and artcritical.</span></p><p class="p1"><span class="s1">Berryhill earne
 d his M.F.A. from Columbia University and has held visiting faculty posit
 ions at Bard\, Columbia\, Pratt\, and VCU. Berryhill was Dean of Skowhe
 gan School of Painting and Sculpture for two years. He was artist-in-resi
 dence at the University of Tennessee\, Knoxville and Virginia Commonwealt
 h University in Richmond\, Virginia and held the Painting's Edge Residenc
 y at Idyllwild Arts Academy in California. He received a New York Foundat
 ion for the Arts Fellowship for Painting and was a Studio Space recipient
  at the Marie Walsh Sharpe Art Foundation.</span></p><p class="p1"><spa
 n class="s1">Born in El Paso\, Texas\, Michael Berryhill earned his und
 ergraduate degree at University of Texas Austin. He lives and works in El
 lenville\, New York.</span></p><p class="p1"><span class="s1"><strong>Art
 ist's instagram:</strong>  @berryhillmichael </span></p>
